const stats = {
  chapters: 10,
  nodes: 22,
  endings: 3,
  sidequests: 6,
  bosses: 8
};

const prevVol = { num: 2, title: 'Specint Espionage & Underground Passages', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-2/` };
const nextVol = { num: 4, title: 'Desert City Cygnus & Gladiator Trials', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-4/` };
---

<WalkthroughLayout
  volume={3}
  volumeTitle="Celestia Alliance & Fortress Battles"
  chapterRange="Chapters 21–30"
  description="Journey through Celestia, battles at Sand Fortress and Judgement Cliff, alliance negotiations, and confrontation with Thaumatech weapons."
  stats={stats}
  quickJumps={quickJumps}
  prevVol={prevVol}
  nextVol={nextVol}
>

  <!-- Chapter 21 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch21"
    number={21}
    title="Sand Fortress (Alternate Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="24" party="Stocke, Raynie, Rosch" enemies={[{"name": "Granorg Archer"}, {"name": "Light Granorgite"}, {"name": "Red Cap"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>_________________
   Sand Fortress N     2F |     B           |     S - Save Point
                          |   ___ ___ ___   |     X - Obstacle
    __       |  |        _|  |   |   |   |  |_    B - Bomb
   /  \     /    \      |    |   |   |B  |  X |   1 - Emerald
  |    |   /      |     |    |   |___|   |  X4|   2 - 2000 G
  |XXXX|  |      /      |_   | 3 |   |   |  X_|   3 - Panacea Plus
  |    |__|     |___      |  |_ _|   |_ _|  |     4 - Mana Crystal x2
  |                7\     |          S      |     5 - Leaf Ring
   \_____     ______/     |______     ______|     6 - Darkshield Scroll
         |   |                   |   |            7 - 2000 G</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>___|   |___          _____ ___________
  3F |           |     1F |   X2|     | B   |
     |          6|        |__ X_|__ __|__ __|
     |___     ___|        | B               |
   ______|   |______      |_____________ ___|     If you have learned the Mana
  |5X   _______     |     |     |     |     |     Sight ability, you can
  |_X___ _____   ___|     |     |_| |_|     |     continue with the plot from
  |B    |_____|     |     |      S        1 |     here.  In addition to the
  |______     ______|     |______     ______|     bombs, you can also find much
         |   |                   |   |            hidden treasure here.</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <p>On the <Tag type="place">1st Floor</Tag>, search the lower right corner for a chest which contains an <Tag type="acc">Emerald</Tag> (Poison Res +6). I&#x27;m not a fan of status resisting equipment, so I would just sell it. Head to the upper right room and search the upper left corner for a white sparkle that is your first bomb to disarm. Go left in the hallway until you find the second bomb. In the upper left room, pull the crates out that block a hidden chest which contains <Tag type="gold">2000 G</Tag>. Now, head up to the <Tag type="place">2nd Floor</Tag>.</p>
      <p>Search the room on the right for a bomb in the upper left corner. The room to the left holds a hidden chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Panacea Plus</Tag>. Leave the room and walk around the back side to find the fourth bomb. On the right side of the floor are some crates that you can pull, blocking a hidden chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Mana Crystals</Tag>. Head up to the <Tag type="place">3rd Floor</Tag>.</p>
      <p>In the upper left corner is the last bomb, but you should still collect some more treasure. Walk around to the right, but don&#x27;t go up the stairs. Pull the crates to the left out of the way that are blocking a chest which contains a <Tag type="acc">Leaf Ring</Tag> (HP+10/MP+10, sell). Climb the stairs and go up to the large room. Search the right side for a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="key">Darkshield Scroll</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>. Don&#x27;t teach to Raynie right now, or you will have to find the bombs all over again.</p>
      <p>Proceed up to the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress North</Tag> area. In the lower right corner is a hidden chest which contains <Tag type="gold">2000 G</Tag>. Now, you should report to <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag> and choose to &quot;Prioritize the Mission&quot; to proceed with the plot, now that the bombs are out of the way.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Knight Stud x2</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Rosch:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">P.Thauma Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Mail Vest</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Wind Armlet</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x2</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Sand Fortress Battle">
        <p>You should know your way around here pretty well by now. I&#x27;d recommend fighting all the enemies you can find on all three floors. Note the soldiers will never spawn in a room. When you&#x27;ve killed enough of them to satisfy your bloodlust, make your way up to the upper room on the third floor to make your last stand. I&#x27;d recommend giving Raynie&#x27;s <Tag type="acc">Horn Charms</Tag> to <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, and having <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> replace her. You may also want to remove Rosch&#x27;s <Tag type="acc">Wind Armlet</Tag>, since you won&#x27;t have a chance to equip it on someone else later.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Grey Shadow, Granorg Archer x2, Light Granorgite" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> The <Tag type="boss">Grey Shadow</Tag> will always start the battle with a <Tag type="skill">Power Zone</Tag>. If anyone steps on it, absolutely get them off of it as quickly as possible or they will kill you. Your first priority should be to take out the Grey Shadow, since that will clear the Power Zone. If you have any full Mana Burst gauges, use <Tag type="skill">Turn Break</Tag> on the Grey Shadow, whenever his turn comes around. In the first round, have <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> use <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on either <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> or <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>. A couple spells and physical attacks should finish him off. The rest can be handled easily without the need for further buffing or healing.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A Message from Home">
        <p>After some cutscenes, you will hear about your next mission.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Knight Stud x2</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 22 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch22"
    number={22}
    title="Sand Fortress (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="27" party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Alistel's Offensive">
        <p>After receiving your objective and destination, talk to <Tag type="char">Viola</Tag> again to advance the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest. Return to the &quot;A New Mission&quot; node. As long as we&#x27;re here, you can teach the <Tag type="key">Darkshield Scroll</Tag> to <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>. Talk to <Tag type="char">Cedric</Tag>, who is on the upper platform next to the tavern. Choosing &quot;Don&#x27;t show journal&quot; will unlock the [A Voice Unheard] ending. Otherwise, choosing to &quot;Show Journal&quot; will complete the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest and you will receive the <Tag type="acc">Noah Amulet</Tag> (Poison/Sleep/Paralysis Res+4, sell).</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Return to &quot;Alistel&#x27;s Offensive&quot; node. Climb up to the third floor and take the north exit to the <Tag type="place">Gran Plain</Tag>.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 23 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch23"
    number={23}
    title="Gran Plain (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="27" party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco" enemies={[{"name": "Blue Granorg Archer", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Granorg Defender"}, {"name": "Hunter", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Rose Balsam", "weakness": "Poison/Stone/Fire"}, {"name": "Sabertooth Tiger"}, {"name": "Wood Shield", "weakness": "Fire"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Battle of Gran Plain">
        <p>Go north one screen, west two, and continue west until you get an update on the battle situation here. You will then have a decision to make. Choosing to &quot;Go north&quot; will unlock [The Lion General] ending.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A Meeting Too Late">
        <p>Before returning to this node, I would strongly recommend resting up in a bed on the second floor of the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress</Tag>. Then, return to the decision point, this time choosing to &quot;Look for Rosch&quot;, and you will find him.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Blue Granorg Archer x3, Paelzan, Wood Shield x3" weakness="Sleep, None, Fire">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> During the first round, use <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>, cast <Tag type="skill">Fire</Tag> on the middle <Tag type="enemy">Wood Shield</Tag>, and cast Magic Boost on <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>. In the second round, <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> <Tag type="boss">Paelzan</Tag> into the <Tag type="enemy">Blue Granorg Archer</Tag> and two Fire spells should finish them off. Next, have <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> heal as necessary, while Stocke and Raynie cast Fire on the Wood Shields. Finally, use <Tag type="skill">Right Assault</Tag> and two Fire spells to finish off the remaining Blue Granorg Archers.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Rosch in Crisis">
        <p>[Wolf in the Fold node] Return to the &quot;Alistel&#x27;s Offensive&quot; node and talk to <Tag type="char">Viola</Tag> to unlock the [Viola&#x27;s Decision] node. Return to the &quot;A Meeting Too Late&quot; node and proceed as before until you are prompted with another decision. Make sure to choose &quot;I leave it to you.&quot;, as this is a requirement to unlocking the sidequest [At Journey&#x27;s End] later.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Lives Entrusted">
        <p>After the battle, the plot will return to <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 24 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch24"
    number={24}
    title="Alistel (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="30" party="Stocke"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Homecoming">
        <p>Before inspecting Hugo&#x27;s office, take the elevator down to the first floor. Talk to the receptionist behind the left desk to receive the [Swordsman Recruit] and [Mercenary Recruit] sidequests, though you won&#x27;t be able to complete them for a very long time. Return to the third floor, and enter Hugo&#x27;s office to the left where you will find someone other than <Tag type="char">Hugo</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Heiss" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to string together four consecutive turns of <Tag type="skill">Fire</Tag> spells to defeat him.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Parting Ways">
        <p>For winning the battle, <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> will learn the <Tag type="skill">Vanish</Tag> technique, that can allow him to sneak past enemies without being seen. This includes the guards back at <Tag type="place">Granorg Palace</Tag>. If you want to go back there now, then skip to GPLC1, but I wouldn&#x27;t do that right now.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Flight">
        <p>Talk to <Tag type="char">Sonja</Tag> in the infirmary to make your escape before you get caught.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Special Forces x2" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> One of them will start with <Tag type="skill">Power Zone</Tag>. Do everything you can to keep them off of it. As long as you do that, they can&#x27;t really hurt you much. Casting <Tag type="skill">Fire</Tag> two or three times is your best bet for killing each of them.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Fiendish">
        <p>After the battle, someone you haven&#x27;t seen before finds you.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 25 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch25"
    number={25}
    title="Celestia (Alternate Chapter 3)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="30" party="Stocke"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix title="Celestia (Alternate Chapter 3) Merchant" items={[{"name": "|2   |             Soothing Balm", "price": 100}, {"name": "|__  |             First Aid Kit", "price": 400}, {"name": "| |             Herbal Tea", "price": 350}, {"name": "Healing Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "_____| |_            Holy Water", "price": 500}, {"name": "|  _   _  | Plaza     Anti-Poison", "price": 50}, {"name": "|1|_   _| |_          Anti-Fear", "price": 50}, {"name": "|___  S_____|         Anti-Paralytic", "price": 50}, {"name": "| |               Anti-Curse", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Sleep", "price": 50}, {"name": "__| |__             Anti-Stone", "price": 50}, {"name": "|3      | Celestia   Poison Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "|       | Entrance   Paralysis Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "Sleep Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "S - Save Point           Curse Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "1 - Crystal Charm        Sleep Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "2 - Anti-Paralytic x2    Stone Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "3 - 3000 G               Power Down", "price": 500}, {"name": "Might Herb", "price": 500}]} equipment={[{"name": "Iron Sword", "price": 2400}, {"name": "Rune Edge", "price": 5000}, {"name": "Iron Lance", "price": 2100}, {"name": "Rune Spear", "price": 2500}, {"name": "Copper Gauntlet", "price": 1700}, {"name": "Red Dagger", "price": 2000}, {"name": "Knife", "price": 1800}, {"name": "Custom Knife", "price": 2800}, {"name": "Heavy Mail", "price": 1500}, {"name": "Silver Mail", "price": 1100}, {"name": "Leather Cuirass", "price": 2000, "note": "buy 1"}, {"name": "Beast Skins", "price": 500}, {"name": "Reinforced Cape", "price": 1200, "note": "buy 1"}, {"name": "Silver Cape", "price": 2800}, {"name": "Hymnal Cape", "price": 3700}, {"name": "Silver Dress", "price": 2000}, {"name": "Charm", "price": 350}, {"name": "Horn Charm", "price": 1000, "note": "buy 4"}, {"name": "Fang Charm", "price": 1000, "note": "buy 3"}, {"name": "Pawn Stud", "price": 750}, {"name": "Knight Stud", "price": 1500}, {"name": "Bishop Stud", "price": 3000, "note": "buy 5"}, {"name": "Seed Ring", "price": 1000}, {"name": "Leaf Ring", "price": 2500}, {"name": "Wind Armlet", "price": 5000}, {"name": "Amber", "price": 1750}, {"name": "Amazonite", "price": 1750}]} itemTitle="Item Shop" equipmentTitle="Equipment Shop" />
      <p>To complete the sidequest, return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node and give the <Tag type="key">Flower Bud</Tag> to the girl on the first floor to advance the [A Flower of Promise] sidequest. Skip to the &quot;A New Mission&quot; node and talk to her again to complete the [A Flower of Promise] sidequest and receive a <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag> (MAG+5/MDF+5). Return to &quot;The Beastkind Forest&quot; node and head up to talk to <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag>.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Unacceptable Loss">
        <p>[Gauntlet node] You will then receive your next mission from Patriarch <Tag type="char">Barranca</Tag>. <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag> will then join your party.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Beastkind's Favor">
        <p>Equip the <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> and <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>. Then, buy a <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag> for Gafka and buy a <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag> for Aht. At this point, I like keeping extra accessories around for different situations, and we have more money than we need, anyway. Buy <Tag type="acc">4 Horn Charms</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">3 Fang Charms</Tag>, and <Tag type="acc">5 Bishop Studs</Tag>. I prefer defensive accessories on Aht for non-boss encounters, despite her Traps being magic-based, since they&#x27;re already more than powerful enough, and she is rather frail. <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> will need to be ready to use magic for the next area, so I like giving him magic-boosting accessories, while keeping Fang Charms in reserve. I&#x27;d also buy 5 Curse &amp; Sleep Wings at the item shop.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Go up to the <Tag type="place">Boundary Tree</Tag> and search the left side for a hidden chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Anti-Paralytics</Tag>. Leave the village via the south entrance, and search the left side for a hidden chest which contains <Tag type="gold">3000 G</Tag>. When you are ready, leave <Tag type="place">Celestia</Tag> and head for <Tag type="place">Lazvil Hills</Tag>.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x2</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 26 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch26"
    number={26}
    title="Lazvil Hills (Alternate Chapter 3)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="30" party="Stocke, Aht, Gafka" enemies={[{"name": "Cloudy", "weakness": "Lightning"}, {"name": "Green Leech", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Rafflesia", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Stompy", "weakness": "Fire"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>Highway         Highway E    Your goal is to defeat the monsters here
                                      that threaten Celestia.  It's a little
                            |X|       tricky, because Aht's speed is so high
          ____________   __/   \      that she really throws off your combos
         X_______   __   _      |     and she has no Assaults for quite some
    ___   |    ____/      |     |     time.  In a pre-emptive strike, you can
   |   |   \  |            \   /      use her extra turn to lay a trap to use
    \  |    | |             |X|       during the following combo chain.  If you
     | |    | |             | |       are fighting a group of Cloudys, have her
                                      cast Polaris to protect against their
    _| |    | |            _| |_      poison.  With magic-boosting accessories,
   |   |   /  |Woodland   |     |     Stocke should be able to one-shot any
    \  |__|   | Path E    | | | |     monster here with Fire.
     |_   ____|          _|/   \|_
_______| |      Southern|___   ___|   There's no more treasure here, if you've
_________|        Path      |X|       already cleared it, as I did back to the
                                      GRNG2 section.  Follow the path to an
                           _| |_      open area, then go north two screens.
S - Save Point    Seaside |     |__   Head west and south one screen to a save
X - Roadblock      Road   |      __   point.  Equip Horn Charms on Stocke, give
                          |_____|     his accessories to Aht, and head west.</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <BossCard name="Forest Bear, Stompy x2" weakness="Ice, Fire">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> These monsters aren&#x27;t a real threat, but your turn queue is probably screwed up. <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> should start by laying an <Tag type="skill">Ice Trap</Tag> for later. However, your first priority should be to take out the two <Tag type="enemy">Stompys</Tag>, before they can summon more help. A <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> from <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag> and <Tag type="skill">Fire</Tag> spell from <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> will do the trick. Push the <Tag type="boss">Forest Bear</Tag> onto the Ice Trap. Then, use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command once to get enough turns to finish off the Forest Bear with two more Ice Traps.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Report from Vanoss">
        <p>You&#x27;ll briefly return to <Tag type="place">Celestia</Tag>. After talking to <Tag type="char">Barranca</Tag>, head to the inn to talk to <Tag type="char">Vanoss</Tag>, and depart for <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x2</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x4</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 27 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch27"
    number={27}
    title="Alistel (Alternate Chapter 3)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="31" party="Stocke, Aht, Gafka" enemies={[{"name": "Alistel Grunt", "weakness": "Sleep"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix title="Alistel (Alternate Chapter 3) Merchant" items={[{"name": "Soothing Balm", "price": 100}, {"name": "First Aid Kit", "price": 400}, {"name": "Herbal Tea", "price": 350}, {"name": "Healing Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "Holy Water", "price": 500}, {"name": "Anti-Poison", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Fear", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Paralytic", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Curse", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Sleep", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Stone", "price": 50}, {"name": "Panacea", "price": 800}, {"name": "Poison Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "Sleep Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "Power Down", "price": 500}, {"name": "Might Herb", "price": 500}]} equipment={[{"name": "Silver Edge", "price": 3000}, {"name": "Iron Sword", "price": 2400}, {"name": "Sorcery Epee", "price": 4600, "note": "buy for Stocke"}, {"name": "Silver Spear", "price": 2000}, {"name": "Iron Lance", "price": 2100}, {"name": "Magic Spear", "price": 3200, "note": "buy for Raynie"}, {"name": "Knife", "price": 1800}, {"name": "Heavy Mail", "price": 1500}, {"name": "Silver Mail", "price": 1100}, {"name": "Silver Cape", "price": 2800}, {"name": "Reinforced Cape", "price": 1200}, {"name": "Gold Clothes", "price": 3200}, {"name": "Charm", "price": 350}, {"name": "Horn Charm", "price": 1000}, {"name": "Pawn Stud", "price": 750}, {"name": "Knight Stud", "price": 1500}, {"name": "Seed Ring", "price": 1000}, {"name": "Breeze Armlet", "price": 1500}]} itemTitle="Item Shop" equipmentTitle="Equipment Shop" />
      <p>Head up, and <Tag type="char">Vanoss</Tag> will arrive.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Darkness in Alistel">
        <p>Talk to <Tag type="char">Vanoss</Tag> again to receive the [Wandering Soul] sidequest. Go up to the <Tag type="place">Second Ward</Tag>, and climb the left stairs to the upper left. Talk to the woman above to receive the [Second Opinion] sidequest. Outside the weapon shop, on the right side of the Second Ward, is a boy to whom you can talk to receive the [Battlefield Missive] sidequest. You should buy a <Tag type="weapon">Sorcery Epee</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> and a <Tag type="weapon">Magic Spear</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> from the shop. Finally, return to the castle north to proceed with the plot.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Reunion with Raul">
        <p>After the meeting, I would continue using <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Gafka</Tag>, and arrange your party as follows. Then, attempt to leave <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Sorcery Epee</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Magic Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Shadow x3" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> should lead with <Tag type="skill">Polaris</Tag> to protect against their Paralysis attack. They may try to complete a formation, in which case, you should break it up with an assault. Otherwise, two of any trap will kill them. If you can, try to get two of them on a single trap to finish them off even more quickly.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>Unless <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> hasn&#x27;t reached Level 30 yet to learn <Tag type="skill">G-Fire</Tag>, I would recommend keeping <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> around and equipping her with the <Tag type="acc">Bishop Studs</Tag> again. Fight the soldiers on your way out of <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>, head to <Tag type="place">Lazvil Hills</Tag>, and follow the same path you took back to <Tag type="place">Celestia</Tag>.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Sorcery Epee</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Magic Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 28 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch28"
    number={28}
    title="Celestia (Alternate Chapter 3)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="33" party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <p>Upon entering, you will find that you are a little late to the party.</p>
      <BossCard name="Alistel Soldier x2, Auto Defender x2" weakness="Sleep, Fire">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Use two <Tag type="item">Sleep Wings</Tag> to crowd control the soldiers. Sadly, the <Tag type="boss">Auto Defenders</Tag> cannot be moved. Have <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> cast <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>. Use Stocke&#x27;s <Tag type="skill">Air Assault</Tag> on one Auto Defender, followed up by <Tag type="skill">G-Fire</Tag> from Raynie to finish it off, and repeat on the second one. Finally, use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to set up a <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag>, Air Assault, G-Fire, and some attacks to finish off the rest.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Premonition of War">
        <p>After some scenes, talk to <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag> at the <Tag type="place">Boundary Tree</Tag>, then return to talk to <Tag type="char">Raul</Tag>. Talk to <Tag type="char">Barranca</Tag> to decide what to do about Alistel and who should lead. Choosing to &quot;Nominate Raul&quot; will unlock the [Assassination of Raul] ending.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Shattered Steel Arm">
        <p>Return to this node and advance the plot up to the same decision. However, choosing to &quot;Nominate Rosch&quot; will only lead to a dead end.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Rosch in Agony">
        <p>If you&#x27;ve already resolved this roadblock, then skip to CLST3. Otherwise, you will need to return to the &quot;How to Disappear&quot; node in Standard History to put the <Tag type="skill">Vanish</Tag> ability to use.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Before doing that, this is as good a time as any to complete those sidequests we got back at <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>. Unfortunately, it will involve going through half of Chapter 3 to get back there to complete them. However, the rewards are good.</p>
      <p>Return to the &quot;A New Mission&quot; node. Climb the stairs by the tavern and talk to the man above to advance the [Second Opinion] sidequest. Return to &quot;The Valkyrie&quot; node and head up to <Tag type="char">Rosch</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Viola</Tag> in the middle room above. Talk to the soldier sitting on the bench to advance the [Battlefield Missive] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="key">Death Pact</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> later. Now for the hard part.</p>
      <p>The nearest node to complete these sidequests is &quot;The Beastkind Forest&quot; node. Advance the plot to the &quot;Darkness in Alistel&quot; node. Talk to the boy by the weapon shop to complete the [Battlefield Missive] sidequest and receive a <Tag type="item">Celestial Oil</Tag>. Head left to the bar. This time, the man will have survived. Talk to him to complete the [Second Opinion] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="key">Slumbering Scroll</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>, which you should teach her immediately. Finally, return to the &quot;How to Disappear&quot; node to continue the plot.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Sorcery Epee</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Magic Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Thaumatech Orb</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Heavy Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rhapsody</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Reinforced Cape</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Gafka:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Claw</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Leather Cuirass</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x6</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 29 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch29"
    number={29}
    title="Granorg Palace (Standard Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="33" party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco" enemies={[{"name": "Blue Granorg Archer", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Granorg Defender"}, {"name": "Heavy Granorgite", "weakness": "Poison/Lightning"}, {"name": "Sand Hunter", "weakness": "Sleep"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>Meeting   Underground   Underground
                         Room       Library        Cell
        Audience  _       ___      ______         ____
          Hall   | |     /   \    |   _  |       |S __|     S - Save Point
